From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yi Xie <imxieyi@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 11:24:15 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] kosmickrisp: implement VK_EXT_image_drm_format_modifier

The Android 2025 baseline that VP_ANDROID_17_requirements inherits makes this
extension mandatory, and the guest Venus driver uses it as the other of the two
conditions for offering VK_ANDROID_native_buffer and the Android hardware
buffer import.

The driver already sized and validated VK_IMAGE_TILING_DRM_FORMAT_MODIFIER_EXT
images: the layout code treats every non-optimal tiling as linear, the image
format query restricts a modifier image to a single 2D level and layer, and its
memory requirements ask for a dedicated allocation. What was missing was the
extension itself, so nothing could ask for one.

Metal describes no tiling an agent outside this driver could agree on, so
DRM_FORMAT_MOD_LINEAR is the only modifier offered, the way lavapipe does it on
a platform without real modifiers. A modifier image is then exactly a linear
image with a name for its layout, and that decides the rest: the modifier is
reported for the formats linear tiling supports, the image format query answers
about linear tiling once it has seen a supported modifier, and an explicit plane
layout is accepted only where it matches the layout Metal's own alignment rule
produces, because this driver cannot lay a texture out any other way.

A modifier image does carry one capability plain linear tiling does not: it can
be a colour attachment. Advertising a modifier that nothing renderable can use
breaks every window system that presents through one, because Mesa's common WSI
filters the modifier list with vkGetPhysicalDeviceImageFormatProperties2 and has
no fallback when nothing survives -- it fails vkCreateSwapchainKHR with
VK_ERROR_OUT_OF_HOST_MEMORY, which dEQP records as a ResourceError that ends the
whole CTS session. Metal renders into a linear texture perfectly well, and this
driver already asks for MTLTextureUsageRenderTarget whenever a linear image is a
transfer destination. What Metal refuses, by an assertion that ends the process,
is a linear texture of any type but MTLTextureType2D, and this driver binds every
input attachment as a 2D array. So a linear layout refuses an input attachment
rather than a colour attachment, plain linear tiling keeps the capabilities it
has always had, and a layout Metal could not represent becomes a Vulkan error
before Metal ever sees the descriptor. kk_linear_layout.h owns that policy and
its Meson test pins it.

The modifier is kept in struct kk_image rather than struct vk_image, whose
drm_format_mod field the common runtime carries only on Linux and the BSDs.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
